From 71fbd0cf1b8be3a155f2377c05ec1ee5cf4c25c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:39:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] For the living: the sheet redrawn in the house style (build
 89 note 11) [HELD FOR HIS OK]

His words: "I want you to revamp this system. It just doesn't really look
good."

components/prayers/NameForm.tsx, from the app's own pieces:
- The name first.
- The relationship as six common words on Settings' carved track (Track),
  or written.
- The nameday from a month and a day, on the same track, or by the saint
  whose feast it is (lib/saints/feastIndex.ts, served as
  /saint-feasts.json and fetched when the choice opens); never typed as
  "MM-DD".
- Tags are gone from the sheet: nothing read them, and a name's own tags
  are kept.
- The note's limit shows only as it nears.
- Save is the house's own button (Button, inverse).

Two house fixes the check found on the way:
- The unlit choices of a carved track read at 3.28:1 on Parchment and 4.54
  on Candlelight; now 62% of the ink, 70% on Parchment (4.5:1 or more on
  all five). Settings and Your rule's switch read better too.
- The shared row (WayRow) had physical padding, 2px off in Arabic; now
  logical.

checkMock passes on all five palettes; the lit choice stands on its raised
plate, which it cannot read, and says so (11:1 or more, measured). New
English words in en.json; the other 20 catalogs follow his OK.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VuYTwbteJqs1UmDUwqRvzC
